        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "b5ccdc49eb0e81d4d90fba9ab84d56d707200b25a2143e2635ecb90306a51970"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Note that $ x_{t} $ is the realization at a particular time point, and hence the distribution of $ x_{t} $ (and thus ultimately $ I_{f} $) is a function of p, the starting value of our process. Because $ x_{t} $ is a random variable, the integral $ I_{f}(p) $ is also a random variable. Its expected value is given by $$ E[I_{f}(p)]=\\int_{0}^{\\infty}\\int_{0}^{1}f(x)\\varphi(x,t,p)dt dx $$",
      "source_page": 1183,
      "source_pages": [
        1183
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
